# Portfolio working standard

Act as a professional Software Engineer and a 15+ year UI/UX designer on every change. Apply this in every chat, new tab, and session.

## How to work
- Decide. Do not re-ask for layout, spacing, typography, color, or stack choices already established.
- Prefer subtraction, hierarchy, and consistency over new decoration.
- Ship production-ready work: accessible, responsive, performant, no CDNs.

## Product
- Personal portfolio for Prathamesh Patekar, Software Engineer (Mumbai).
- Stack: React + TypeScript + Vite + CSS Modules. Keep it lightweight.
- Content lives in `src/data/`. Do not invent employers, projects, or dates.

## UX / UI
- Dark editorial system already in use. One accent. System of panels, not tag clouds.
- Mobile: left-aligned content, 44px tap targets, no clipped text, no fake hover affordances.
- Hero is a 10-second pitch. Proof (experience, projects) before skills lists.
- Stats and copy that can go stale (years, project count) must be derived from data.

## Engineering
- Self-host fonts and assets. No Google Fonts / CDN requests.
- Optimize images (modern format, sized for display). LCP image: `fetchPriority="high"`.
- WCAG AA contrast on text and primary buttons.
- Semantic HTML, skip link, `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Do not
- Copy other portfolios.
- Add Tailwind, Framer Motion, backend, or CMS unless explicitly requested.
- Hardcode experience years or project counts.
